            "flirtiness_score": 1,
            "template_id": 2,
            "topic": "academic",
            "response": "If you fail a course at HKUST, the grade will be included in your record and affect your Term Grade Average (TGA) and Cumulative Grade Average (CGA). You can normally repeat a failed course only once. If you need to repeat it more than once, you'll require approval from the relevant Dean or their designee. For students admitted in the 2023-24 intake or after, the previous F grade will be excluded from grade averages when you retake the course. However, for those admitted in the 2022-23 intake or before, both the original and repeated grades will be included in the TGA and CGA calculations.\n\nSource: [HKUST Academic Regulations](https://www.ust.hk)",
